            <div xml:id="d73">

                <pb facs="0182" n="72" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg72"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/4263: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hawks</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-10-19T11:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 19,
                                1928—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 1 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>118. Honduran Minister informs me that General Jeffries is aiding Honduran <hi
                        rendition="#italic">emigrados</hi> in revolutionary activities. He requests
                    that Jeffries be deported to the United States or at least concentrated here
                    under police surveillance. Please instruct immediately whether I should make
                    such request of the Government of Guatemala. I recommend that one of the two
                    courses be taken.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hawks</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
